Z||000021||blade56_2001||04-15-2001||04:02 AM||||I was getting about 5 miles to the gallon and I had a little problem with engine coolant temp sensor not doing it's job and melting all of my plug wires and radiator hoses. while I was replacing them I decided to rip off the upper plenum (86-2m6se)and as I did that I found that the EGR tube that connects from the EGR valve to the upper plenum was busted at the plenum so talk about a huge vacuum leak! that will eat your gas quick. I found the part at the gm dealer for $79.00 (YEAH, At the dealership) everyone else including <A HREF="http://www.fierostore.com" TARGET=_blank>www.fierostore.com</A>  wanted $100.00. and the only way to tell if it's busted is to remove the upper plenum. So check that out.<P>That's my two cents.||||reg||1
